Privacy Policy

Last Updated: September 12, 2026

Toygurt ("we", "our", or "us") operates the mobile game LittleBall Run: 3D Ball Runner (the "Game").

This Privacy Policy explains how information is handled when you use the Game.

1. Information We Collect

We do not directly collect or store personal information from users.

The Game does not require you to create an account and does not ask you to provide information such as your name, email address, phone number, or physical address.

However, the Game may use third-party advertising services to display advertisements. These services may automatically collect certain information from your device for purposes such as displaying and measuring advertisements, preventing fraud, and improving advertising services.

The information collected by third-party advertising providers is handled according to their own privacy policies.

2. Advertising

The Game contains advertisements provided by third-party advertising services.

Advertising providers may collect and use information such as advertising identifiers, device information, approximate location, and information about interactions with advertisements, depending on their services and applicable laws.

We do not directly collect or store this information.

For more information about how advertising providers handle data, please refer to the privacy policy of the relevant advertising provider.

3. In-App Purchases

The Game offers an optional one-time in-app purchase.

Payments are processed through Google Play. We do not receive or store your payment card information or other payment details.

Google may process information necessary to complete and manage your purchase in accordance with its own privacy policies and terms.

4. Children's Privacy

LittleBall Run: 3D Ball Runner is intended to be suitable for children under the age of 13.

We do not knowingly collect personal information directly from children.

Because the Game may display advertisements, advertising services may process certain device or advertising-related information. We take steps to use advertising services in accordance with applicable children's privacy and advertising requirements.

5. Third-Party Services

The Game may use third-party services, including advertising and payment services.

These third parties may collect information in accordance with their own privacy policies. We recommend reviewing their policies for more information about their data practices.

6. Data Security

We do not directly collect or maintain personal information through the Game. However, no method of electronic transmission or storage is completely secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.

7. Data Retention

Because we do not directly collect or store personal information, we do not maintain a database of users' personal information.

Third-party service providers may retain information according to their own policies and applicable laws.

8. Your Rights

Depending on your location and applicable law, you may have rights regarding personal information processed by third-party service providers, including rights to access, delete, or restrict the use of certain information.

For requests concerning data processed by third-party services, you may need to contact the relevant service provider directly.

9. Changes to This Privacy Policy

We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time.

Any changes will be reflected by updating the "Last Updated" date at the top of this Privacy Policy. We encourage you to review this Privacy Policy periodically.

10. Contact Us

If you have any questions about this Privacy Policy or the Game's privacy practices, please contact us at:

Email: toygurtcraft@gmail.com

Developer: Toygurt

